            <ArticleTitle>Haemoglobin A1, blood glucose, and high-density lipoprotein cholesterol in insulin-requiring diabetics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>547-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In forty insulin-requiring diabetics there was a significant correlation between haemoglobin A1 (HbA1) and blood-glucose measured at the same time and mean clinic blood-glucose measured over the previous year. There was no significant correlation between high-density lipoprotein (H.D.L.) cholesterol concentration and HbA1 or blood-glucose. HbA1 is not a good predictor of H.D.L. cholesterol concentration in insulin-requiring diabetics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
